course: dictionary
lesson: 3454
title: Faeces: the body's solid waste
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Your body takes in food, uses the parts it needs, and gets rid of what is left over. Scientists call this left-over solid waste faeces, which is the word for poo. «What is left goes into the large intestine, where water is taken back into the body, and the waste leaves the body as faeces.» So the body takes water back from the waste first, and then the dry leftovers leave through the bottom.
explain: Faeces is a plural-looking word, but we use it as one thing, like the word rice. In America the spelling is feces. Both spellings mean the same thing. In a science lesson you will use the word faeces; at home and with friends you might say poo.
explain: Animals make faeces too. A cow's faeces is called dung, and many animals leave droppings. Scientists can look at droppings to find out which animals live in an area, so this waste is useful to them as well as gross.
fact: Faeces is solid waste that leaves the body through the bottom.
fact: Faeces is the scientific word for poo.
fact: Faeces carry germs, so we wash our hands after using the toilet.
fact: Droppings is the word for animal faeces, and dung is the word for the faeces of large animals such as cows and horses.
fact: In the UK people say poo, and in the US people often say poop. The American spelling is feces.
exercise: «What is left goes into the large intestine, where water is taken back into the body, and the waste leaves the body as faeces.» What does faeces mean? | Food that is being chewed | *Solid waste that leaves the body through the bottom | Air breathed out from the lungs | Water that the body takes back in
exercise: Which common word is used in the UK for faeces? | Pebble | *Poo | Puddle
exercise: Why do we wash our hands after using the toilet? | Because toilet water is warm | Because soap makes hands shiny | *Because faeces can carry germs | Because hands look dirty
test: What can animal droppings help scientists find out? | The time of day | The colour of the sky | *Which animals live nearby
test: Which word is used for the faeces of large animals such as cows and horses? | *Dung | Shells | Fur | Feathers
exam: In the body, where does the waste go before it leaves as faeces? | The brain | The lungs | *The large intestine | The heart
